name whoever empties a table selection, and what a draw was told

A row that is selected and then silently deselected looks EXACTLY like a highlight that was never
painted, and the two want opposite fixes. Task #210 spent two rounds on the second reading before
these four traces showed it was the first.

drawRect: fills the background unconditionally and draws the highlight only behind a row count and a
non-empty selection, so a draw that finds neither wipes the highlight and puts nothing back. The
draw line prints the view POINTER, because the finding is two draws of the SAME table minutes apart
answering differently:

  CIDER_TABLE draw IATableView_Aspects_ 0x73ff7027d190 clip=295x524+0+0 rows=4 selected=1
  CIDER_TABLE draw IATableView_Aspects_ 0x73ff7027d190 clip=295x524+0+0 rows=4 selected=0

_setSelectedRowIndexes: takes a backtrace when a non-empty selection is replaced by an empty one,
which named the culprit in one run as iA Writer itself via __NSFireDelayedPerform.

clickedRow prints its answer because an application that overrides mouseDown: and sends its own
action reads it to decide what the click meant, so a wrong answer here is indistinguishable from the
application ignoring the click. iA Writer got 3, correctly, and deselected anyway.

rowViewAtRow: prints when it is asked. Across a launch and a click iA Writer asks ZERO times, which
is the measurement that sets how much of #211 is worth building.

All four are on CIDER_TRACE_CONTROL beside the mouseDown, selectedRow and highlight lines already
here. The gate tests for a non-empty value, not merely a set one, because drivers export every
switch and an empty value would turn them all on.

